    <p>A play is a story written to be acted for an audience. Its elements are theme (message), characters (including protagonist and antagonist), plot (exposition, rising action, climax, falling action, resolution), conflict (the problem), resolution (how it ends), setting (where and when) and language (dialogue and style).</p>
