    <div style="background:#3e2723;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #f48fb1;margin-bottom:20px;">
    <h3 style="color:#e8eaf6;margin-top:0;">🧠 Lesson Summary</h3>
    <p>The grand stave joins the treble and bass staves, with middle C between them. A dot adds half a note’s value (dotted minim = 3, dotted crotchet = 1½); a quaver is ½; each has a matching rest. A tie joins two notes of the same pitch. Note extension shows exact lengths and lets notes cross bar lines. In 4/4 time each bar has four crotchet beats. F major is F G A B♭ C D E F, with tonic arpeggio F A C F.</p>
    <h4 style="color:#e8eaf6;margin:16px 0 6px 0;">🗒️ Revision notes</h4>
    <ul style="margin:6px 0;padding-left:22px;">
    <li>Grand stave.</li>
    <li>Dots and ties.</li>
    <li>4/4.</li>
    <li>F major.</li>
    </ul>
    </div>
